    "description": "### Impact\r\n\r\nThe `allowed_spam_host_domains` check used `String#end_with?` without domain boundary validation, allowing domains like `attacker-example.com` to bypass spam protection when `example.com` was allowlisted.\r\n\r\nRequire exact match or proper subdomain match (preceded by `.`) to prevent suffix-based bypass of `newuser_spam_host_threshold`.\r\n\r\n### Workarounds\r\n\r\nUpgrade to the patched version.",
